# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Add storage invariant checks to pallet-psm try_state

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `pallet-psm` has a `do_try_state` function with five checks. This PR
      increases that number to seventeen. The `try_state` hook calls the function
      with the `try-runtime` feature. The checks confirm that each reserve covers
      the debt against it, that the issuance of the internal asset covers the debt
      of the instance, that no row stays after the removal of its PSM, and that no
      debt exists for a pair that the PSM does not approve.

      Five checks are advisory. An advisory check writes a warning to the log,
      and it does not return an error. A permitted action can create each of
      these states. Governance can set debt above a per-asset ceiling, debt
      above the ceiling of an instance, and a reserve with a balance but with
      zero weight and zero debt. An asset owner can change asset metadata, so
      live decimals that differ from the values recorded at registration are
      warnings: swaps use the recorded values, and the arithmetic of the pallet
      does not depend on live metadata.
      Fee and weight rows for a pair that the PSM does not approve are hard
      errors, because no extrinsic can create them and a stray weight row
      shrinks the ceilings of the approved assets.

      Each check has a unit test. A test changes one storage item, then it confirms
      the specific error. A test of an advisory check confirms the result is `Ok`.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: minor
